     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dear forum,</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <span lang=\"EN-US\">I’m trying\r\nto create a graph with ggplot2, which combines boxplots with jitter plots. I\r\nknow that you can plot both together using “ geom=c(&quot;boxplot&quot;,\r\n&quot;jitter&quot;)”. But in my dataset some cases have &gt;50 datapoints (and\r\nallow to create a meaningful boxplot), but some other cases (from published\r\npapers) only have 1 to 4 observations. For the latter, a jitter plot is most\r\nappropriate, as some values are identical. Now I want to combine this into one\r\nplot. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<pre><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">&gt; </span></span><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">head(D)</span></span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\"><span>    </span>Case Length Source</span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">1 Case_A<span>   </span>29.5<span>      </span>O</span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">2 Case_A<span>   </span>30.0<span>      </span>O</span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">3 Case_A<span>   </span>29.5<span>      </span>O</span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">4 Case_A<span>   </span>31.0<span>      </span>O</span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">5 Case_A<span>   </span>30.0<span>      </span>O</span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">6 Case_A<span>   </span>31.0<span>      </span>O</span></pre><pre><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">&gt; </span></span><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">tail(D)</span></span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\"><span>     </span>Case Length Source</span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">54 Case_C<span>     </span>26<span>      </span>L</span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">55 Case_C<span>     </span>24<span>      </span>L</span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">56 Case_C<span>     </span>24<span>      </span>L</span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">57 Case_C<span>     </span>23<span>      </span>L</span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">58 Case_D<span>     </span>27<span>      </span>L</span></pre><pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;background:#e1e2e5\" lang=\"EN-US\">59 Case_D<span>     </span>26<span>      </span>L</span></pre>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">The example\r\nbelow shows the graph with both boxplot and jitterplot for all cases, but I\r\nwould like to see:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:53.4pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Wingdings\" lang=\"EN-US\"><span>--<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"> </span></span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\">only the boxplot for Case_A and\r\nCase_B (Source = O =observations)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:53.4pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Wingdings\" lang=\"EN-US\"><span>--<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\"></span></span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\">, and only the jitter plot for\r\nCase_C and Case_D (Source = L = from literature).</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span><img alt=\"\"></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Any\r\nsuggestions?</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Best\r\nwishes,</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">K.</span></p>\r\n\r\n</div>"
